 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "wait[i] >= 1 is the longest time process i (queued in index order) may wait. At time 0 all processes are in the queue. At each second t = 1, 2, ...: the process at the front of the queue is processed and removed, and at the same moment every remaining process with wait <= t is removed. Return the queue sizes at times 0, 1, 2, ... up to and including the first time the queue is empty (for an empty input, [0]).",
  "provenance": [
